==English==
{{was wotd|2018|June|23}}

===Etymology===
[[File:Hickman line catheter with 2 lumens.jpg|thumb|A {{w|Hickman line}}, a central [[venous]] catheter used when [[long-term]] [[intravenous]] [[access#Noun|access]] is required for [[chemotherapy]], [[dialysis]], or other uses]]

Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|cathéter}}, from {{der|en|grc|καθετήρ||surgical instrument for emptying the bladder}}, from {{m|grc|καθίημι||to descend, let down}} + {{m|grc|-τήρ||''suffix forming masculine nouns from verbs''}} (from {{der|en|ine-pro|*-tḗr||''suffix forming {{glossary|agent nouns}} from verbs, denoting someone or something whose role or purpose it is to perform the verb's action''}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈkæθɪtə(ɹ)/|lang=en}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|/ˈkæθɪt̬ɚ/|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|ca|the|ter|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|medicine}} A small [[tube]] [[insert#Verb|inserted]] into a [[body]] [[cavity]] to [[administer]] a [[drug#Noun|drug]], [[create]] an [[opening#Noun|opening]], [[distend]] a [[passageway]], or [[remove#Verb|remove]] [[fluid]].

